  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "On average, gpt-5.3-instant scores above gpt-5.1-instant and below gpt-5.2-instant on disallowed-content [Production Benchmarks](/evals/openai-production-benchmarks).", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 3,
        "quote": "On average, the model performs above gpt-5.1-instant and below gpt-5.2-instant on our disallowed"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "gpt-5.3-instant regresses vs gpt-5.2-instant and gpt-5.1-instant on disallowed sexual content, and vs gpt-5.2-instant on self-harm (standard and dynamic).", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 3,
        "quote": "gpt-5.3-instant shows regressions relative to gpt-5.2-instant and gpt-5.1-\ninstant for disallowed sexual content"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Online experimentation did not show an increase in undesirable self-harm responses despite offline self-harm regressions.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 3,
        "quote": "did not observe an increase in undesirable responses for self-harm"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "ChatGPT deploys system-level safeguards intended to mitigate disallowed sexual content.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 3,
        "quote": "we deploy system-level safeguards in ChatGPT intended to mitigate\nthis behavior"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Ahead of launch, OpenAI added dynamic multi-turn evaluations for mental health, emotional reliance, and self-harm.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "2",
        "pdfPage": 3,
        "quote": "we implemented dynamic multi-turn evaluations for\nmental health, emotional reliance, and self-harm"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to GPT-5.2 Instant, GPT-5.3 Instant is slightly worse on [HealthBench](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.08775) at nearly matched average length.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "3",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "scores 54.1% on HealthBench (-1.3%), 25.9% on\nHard (-0.9%), and 95.3% on Consensus (-0.5%)"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On [HealthBench](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.08775) consensus criteria, strengths include better context-seeking (+4.4%) and hedging (+4.0%) vs GPT-5.2 Instant.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "3",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "better context-seeking when important information is missing (+4.4%)"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On [HealthBench](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.08775) consensus criteria, weaknesses include seeking context before referral (-10.1%) and local healthcare-context accuracy (-5.5%).", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "3",
        "pdfPage": 4,
        "quote": "poorer behavior in seeking context before referral (-10.1%)"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The card says the comprehensive safety mitigation approach is largely the same as for GPT-5.2 Instant in the GPT-5.2 System Card.", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "1",
        "pdfPage": 2,
        "quote": "safety mitigation approach for this model is largely\nthe same as that described for GPT-5.2 Instant in the GPT-5.2 System Card"
      }
    }
  ],
